  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "v1.3.0 - The accent re-ramp.\n\nAccent states now darken on interaction instead of lightening. That lets accent text, checkmarks and radio dots be light and crisp while clearing WCAG AA on every state (4.53 / 7.32 / 10.50). Orange moves off the pressed fill onto the border and a new press glow.\n\nContrast fixes in both themes: the dark hover tint no longer washes out the text sitting on it, and placeholder and muted label text are now readable on glass panels and on hovered controls.\n\nUpgrades to Avalonia 12.1.3.\n\nNo migration needed - nothing renamed or removed, same single StyleInclude entry point, still net10.0. Accent and checked controls do look different: they darken on hover rather than lightening, and their text is light rather than dark.",
